WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.000
The program runs
coexistence on five rules.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.612
One issuer at a time for each
use case and population.

3
00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:08.974
Trust goes up before issuance moves.

4
00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:12.425
Revocation is reachable
wherever validation happens.

5
00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:17.237
Nothing is revoked just to force a move;
certificates are replaced at renewal.

6
00:00:17.237 --> 00:00:19.638
And every move has a tested rollback.

7
00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:23.419
Some things stay on AD CS
until Active Directory retires,

8
00:00:23.419 --> 00:00:26.638
like domain controller
and LDAPS certificates;

9
00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:31.949
the old guide said LDAPS could move to Cloud
PKI, but an LDAPS endpoint is a server.

10
00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:37.525
RADIUS needs special care, because it must
trust both chains for the whole overlap.

11
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:43.146
And trust runs both ways: the AD CS
chain into Entra ID, and the cloud chain

12
00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:48.910
into each forest, with NTAuth only
for CAs that issue logon certificates.
